1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,584
They brought the kid here just recently.

2
00:00:02,584 --> 00:00:05,572
And based on our records, he's now an orphan.

3
00:00:05,572 --> 00:00:07,607
Do you know the kid's parents?

4
00:00:07,607 --> 00:00:12,645
I thought he was here
because he got separated from his parents.

5
00:00:12,645 --> 00:00:13,880
It turns out he's an orphan.

6
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:17,050
You can remove me from this project,
but retain Joyce.

7
00:00:17,050 --> 00:00:21,353
Joyce will stay in the project
if you return to Casa Fuerte.

8
00:00:22,222 --> 00:00:24,624
Liam is not working at Blacksmith anymore.

9
00:00:24,624 --> 00:00:25,859
He's going back to Casa Fuerte.

10
00:00:25,859 --> 00:00:27,627
You resigned at Blacksmith?

11
00:00:27,627 --> 00:00:28,895
What about our movie?

12
00:00:28,895 --> 00:00:30,296
I don't have a choice, Joyce.

13
00:00:30,296 --> 00:00:34,166
If there's something I learned
in making our film,

14
00:00:34,167 --> 00:00:36,875
that is we all have a choice.

15
00:00:36,876 --> 00:00:39,913
You taught me how to be brave.

16
00:00:39,913 --> 00:00:43,550
But I went overboard. I did Via wrong.

17
00:00:43,550 --> 00:00:45,318
Don't blame yourself.

18
00:00:45,318 --> 00:00:48,254
I have no one else to blame but myself.

19
00:00:48,254 --> 00:00:50,256
And I think you should also do that.

20
00:00:50,256 --> 00:00:52,759
Take full accountability
for all of your decisions.

21
00:00:52,759 --> 00:00:55,061
Are you having an affair with my boyfriend?

22
00:00:55,061 --> 00:00:57,363
Nothing's going on between me and Liam.

23
00:00:57,363 --> 00:00:58,832
He called me Joyce.

24
00:00:58,832 --> 00:01:00,867
I didn't know who Joyce was.

25
00:01:00,867 --> 00:01:04,436
Until I found out that you are Joyce.

26
00:01:27,627 --> 00:01:29,629
Could it be Sir Liam?

27
00:01:29,629 --> 00:01:31,263
I hope so.

28
00:02:03,463 --> 00:02:04,862
How's everyone doing?

29
00:02:04,862 --> 00:02:08,968
Here's the script from Liam...

30
00:02:09,681 --> 00:02:12,213
His final input for the film.

31
00:02:34,363 --> 00:02:37,399
What's taking him so long?

32
00:02:37,399 --> 00:02:39,001
Liam doesn't get late, my friend.

33
00:02:39,001 --> 00:02:40,768
I'm sure he's on his way.

34
00:03:06,161 --> 00:03:08,363
We can now start!

35
00:03:08,363 --> 00:03:10,865
Our creative manager is here.

36
00:03:26,281 --> 00:03:28,116
What are you doing here?

37
00:03:28,116 --> 00:03:30,184
Does Dad know you're here?

38
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:34,222
I will finish what I started.

39
00:03:35,857 --> 00:03:38,259
You really have gone crazy.

40
00:03:41,730 --> 00:03:45,366
Liam, you are going against
Congressman Ramon.

41
00:03:46,068 --> 00:03:48,637
VLH, let's talk about that later.

42
00:03:48,637 --> 00:03:50,105
I'm busy.

43
00:03:50,105 --> 00:03:54,075
The set is ready, Sir Liam.

44
00:03:55,811 --> 00:03:59,380
Sir Liam, let's start filming.

45
00:04:08,723 --> 00:04:10,112
Vergil.

46
00:04:12,594 --> 00:04:14,462
Okay, thank you.

47
00:04:19,734 --> 00:04:22,536
Liam is at the shooting.

48
00:04:24,339 --> 00:04:27,241
Your son is messing with me!

49
00:04:46,862 --> 00:04:48,356
Go on!

50
00:05:10,418 --> 00:05:13,220
Chito... Chito!

51
00:05:14,589 --> 00:05:15,991
Chito?

52
00:05:21,995 --> 00:05:24,064
Chito!

53
00:05:24,064 --> 00:05:26,066
Chito, hold on. Wake up.

54
00:05:26,066 --> 00:05:27,734
Wake up. We'll go home together.

55
00:05:27,734 --> 00:05:30,237
We'll go home to our town.

56
00:05:30,237 --> 00:05:31,838
Chito...

57
00:05:31,838 --> 00:05:34,574
Chito... Chito, wait...

58
00:05:34,574 --> 00:05:36,543
I love you so much.

59
00:05:37,502 --> 00:05:40,297
Chito, I love you so much.

60
00:05:41,048 --> 00:05:43,615
Chito!

61
00:05:48,021 --> 00:05:51,774
Sir Liam, why did you kill the hero?

62
00:05:51,774 --> 00:05:53,459
They're still filming.

63
00:06:00,434 --> 00:06:02,202
Chito!

64
00:06:02,202 --> 00:06:03,537
Cut!

65
00:06:03,537 --> 00:06:05,072
Good take.

66
00:06:05,072 --> 00:06:06,406
Lovely!

67
00:06:06,406 --> 00:06:08,875
- Perfect.
- Wow.

68
00:06:08,875 --> 00:06:11,011
PA, please assist the actors. Hurry!

69
00:06:11,011 --> 00:06:12,245
Makeup, tissue!

70
00:06:12,245 --> 00:06:14,681
Good job, guys.

71
00:06:14,681 --> 00:06:16,184
Good job.

72
00:06:18,719 --> 00:06:20,987
Odet, water, please.

73
00:06:25,525 --> 00:06:27,694
Okay.

74
00:06:27,694 --> 00:06:29,195
Great.

75
00:06:31,698 --> 00:06:33,912
Show them the fight scene. How is it done?

76
00:06:39,373 --> 00:06:41,108
Don't!

77
00:06:41,108 --> 00:06:43,910
- Why?
- I'm better than you, Sir Liam.

78
00:06:43,910 --> 00:06:47,547
My mom told me to eat my vegetables.

79
00:06:47,547 --> 00:06:49,080
And I'm an obedient boy.

80
00:06:49,080 --> 00:06:50,283
So what?

81
00:06:50,283 --> 00:06:51,451
You can make me eat anything except for that.

82
00:06:51,451 --> 00:06:52,753
Eat it!

83
00:06:52,753 --> 00:06:53,954
I don't want that.

84
00:06:53,954 --> 00:06:56,123
- Go and eat that.
- You eat it.

85
00:06:56,123 --> 00:06:57,724
No. You eat first.

86
00:06:57,724 --> 00:06:59,459
You eat it.

87
00:06:59,459 --> 00:07:00,660
Ouch!

88
00:07:00,660 --> 00:07:02,062
Sorry!

89
00:07:02,062 --> 00:07:04,564
Sorry. It's your fault. You're so stubborn.

90
00:07:04,564 --> 00:07:05,632
I said eat this.

91
00:07:05,632 --> 00:07:09,002
- I said no.
- What's happening here?

92
00:07:09,002 --> 00:07:13,573
Sir Liam doesn't want to eat okra.

93
00:07:13,573 --> 00:07:16,743
You don't eat okra?

94
00:07:16,743 --> 00:07:18,811
I can't eat it.

95
00:07:19,413 --> 00:07:21,181
Have you eaten yet? Finish your food.

96
00:07:21,181 --> 00:07:22,649
I eat okra.

97
00:07:22,649 --> 00:07:24,184
- Let me see if you really eat okra.
- Sit here.

98
00:07:24,184 --> 00:07:26,428
You're forcing Liam to eat it.

99
00:07:26,428 --> 00:07:28,922
- Eat up.
- Eat this first.

100
00:07:28,922 --> 00:07:31,040
Show us that you eat it.

101
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:34,594
- He's not eating it.
- Let's see if you eat vegetables.

102
00:07:34,594 --> 00:07:36,463
Ready?

103
00:07:41,301 --> 00:07:44,838
- I don't want it!
- Eat it.

104
00:07:44,838 --> 00:07:46,387
- Eat it!
- Don't spit it out.

105
00:07:46,387 --> 00:07:49,309
Eat it.

106
00:07:49,309 --> 00:07:51,412
Go on.

107
00:07:54,614 --> 00:07:56,983
It's good, right?

108
00:07:56,983 --> 00:07:58,151
It's good, isn't it?

109
00:07:58,151 --> 00:07:59,685
Gosh.

110
00:08:00,287 --> 00:08:03,056
Do you really have to be fed
before you eat it?

111
00:08:03,056 --> 00:08:04,691
How about you?

112
00:08:04,691 --> 00:08:06,292
Gosh.

113
00:08:08,895 --> 00:08:10,163
One more, one more.

114
00:08:10,163 --> 00:08:11,898
No! I don't want it anymore.

115
00:08:11,898 --> 00:08:12,966
One is enough.

116
00:08:12,966 --> 00:08:15,935
Here you go, Sep. Eat your food.

117
00:08:23,410 --> 00:08:25,945
What's gotten into you?
Why did you come back?

118
00:08:28,682 --> 00:08:29,850
Okra?

119
00:08:33,753 --> 00:08:35,888
Seriously.

120
00:08:38,391 --> 00:08:42,028
It means you chose this. Our film.

121
00:08:51,446 --> 00:08:53,173
No, stop.

122
00:08:53,173 --> 00:08:55,442
Stop. I don't want it anymore.

123
00:08:55,442 --> 00:08:57,377
You should do this.

124
00:08:59,112 --> 00:09:00,680
Hey, hey.

125
00:09:00,680 --> 00:09:01,681
No!

126
00:09:01,681 --> 00:09:03,216
I don't want it!

127
00:09:03,216 --> 00:09:04,451
Eat it.

128
00:09:04,451 --> 00:09:06,286
I don't want it anymore.

129
00:09:06,286 --> 00:09:08,020
Come on!

130
00:09:09,523 --> 00:09:11,357
I knew you'd be here.

131
00:09:13,894 --> 00:09:16,897
My dad called. He is furious.

132
00:09:16,897 --> 00:09:19,335
You didn't show up for your meeting.

133
00:09:23,645 --> 00:09:28,207
Yeah, I'll explain it to Dad and Uncle Ramon.

134
00:09:34,915 --> 00:09:35,982
Hi.

135
00:09:35,982 --> 00:09:39,886
Are you Sir Liam's friend, too?

136
00:09:39,886 --> 00:09:44,523
I'm Sep. I'm his friend from the orphanage.

137
00:09:50,163 --> 00:09:52,064
I'm Via.

138
00:09:52,933 --> 00:09:55,935
I'm Liam's girlfriend.

139
00:10:13,286 --> 00:10:15,255
Come on, let's eat.

140
00:10:15,255 --> 00:10:16,611
I'm okay.

141
00:10:24,038 --> 00:10:27,322
What's the update about the delivery
of the explosives?

142
00:10:27,322 --> 00:10:29,435
They said it's almost here.

143
00:10:30,370 --> 00:10:33,773
I'll wait for it.
The Director might need you.

144
00:10:33,773 --> 00:10:36,809
- They've started rolling already.
- Okay, Sir Liam.

145
00:10:51,891 --> 00:10:54,460
- Who are you?
- Don't run.

146
00:10:55,362 --> 00:10:57,676
- Who are you?
- Don't move!

147
00:11:08,375 --> 00:11:10,009
Liam!

148
00:11:17,550 --> 00:11:19,151
Who are you?

149
00:13:55,415 --> 00:13:57,049
Uncle Ramon.

150
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:15,260
What's the meaning of this?

151
00:14:32,946 --> 00:14:35,319
Looks like you already made a decision.

152
00:14:37,251 --> 00:14:45,159
Now, it's my turn to decide.

153
00:15:33,507 --> 00:15:35,592
You're scared of the bullet,

154
00:15:36,720 --> 00:15:40,141
but you're not scared of messing with me.

155
00:15:43,684 --> 00:15:48,121
What happened to our agreement that
you'd be returning to Casa Fuerte?

156
00:15:54,261 --> 00:15:56,195
I can't.

157
00:15:58,297 --> 00:16:01,466
I can't just do everything you say.

158
00:16:03,370 --> 00:16:08,909
You're making me do bad things for money!

159
00:16:20,955 --> 00:16:23,291
We only need two tires.

160
00:16:23,291 --> 00:16:28,462
Two tires and a can of kerosene.

161
00:16:30,364 --> 00:16:33,600
Your mother will mourn over your ashes.

162
00:16:38,906 --> 00:16:42,109
I love being on top.

163
00:16:44,712 --> 00:16:49,216
It feels different when you have the power.

164
00:16:50,551 --> 00:16:52,386
What a waste.

165
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:55,755
Better luck next time.

166
00:17:07,134 --> 00:17:09,408
Dad, stop!

167
00:17:16,077 --> 00:17:18,258
What are you doing here?

168
00:17:36,429 --> 00:17:37,857
Via.

169
00:17:38,900 --> 00:17:42,201
Passengers getting off at Husena...
this is your stop.

170
00:17:42,201 --> 00:17:44,069
Get off. Hurry up.

171
00:17:44,069 --> 00:17:46,366
Is there anyone else?

172
00:17:50,476 --> 00:17:52,687
I can't let you do this.

173
00:17:53,443 --> 00:17:56,053
I love him, Dad.

174
00:18:32,714 --> 00:18:34,327
Time to get off.

175
00:18:34,327 --> 00:18:36,829
This is the last stop.

176
00:18:47,678 --> 00:18:50,203
Has everyone already gotten off?

177
00:19:16,071 --> 00:19:17,694
Bad day?

178
00:19:25,841 --> 00:19:28,977
I don't believe Friday the 13th is bad luck.

179
00:19:30,476 --> 00:19:33,846
But I think it might be true today.

180
00:19:33,846 --> 00:19:39,151
I escaped the hustle and bustle of the city

181
00:19:39,752 --> 00:19:43,803
so I can at least breathe...

182
00:19:43,803 --> 00:19:45,681
So I can unwind.

183
00:19:49,687 --> 00:19:51,765
Wow!

184
00:19:51,765 --> 00:19:54,005
The view is breathtaking.

185
00:20:04,703 --> 00:20:13,734
This is the kind of view that goes unnoticed
during our trips.

186
00:20:19,959 --> 00:20:23,694
Unseen scenery.

187
00:20:34,490 --> 00:20:36,992
How would you know...

188
00:20:39,916 --> 00:20:42,874
if there's another chance?

189
00:20:47,422 --> 00:20:49,721
That even for once...

190
00:20:51,426 --> 00:20:53,356
you'll get noticed?

191
00:20:55,295 --> 00:20:57,952
What are you talking about?

192
00:20:58,798 --> 00:21:03,202
I can clearly see you, because of that.

193
00:21:04,204 --> 00:21:05,437
What?

194
00:21:06,180 --> 00:21:09,777
I can see you clearly
because of your red shoes.

195
00:21:09,777 --> 00:21:11,513
It's so bloody red.

196
00:21:11,513 --> 00:21:16,017
And the heels are too high.
How can I not notice you?

197
00:21:16,649 --> 00:21:24,800
You can't move forward
if all the weight is on your shoes.

198
00:21:28,790 --> 00:21:30,382
Look at this.

199
00:21:36,430 --> 00:21:37,778
Look.

200
00:21:39,207 --> 00:21:42,366
See? It feels so light.

201
00:21:43,474 --> 00:21:44,745
Right?

202
00:21:45,626 --> 00:21:47,304
Go on, Miss. Try it.

203
00:21:47,304 --> 00:21:49,738
Try to take your red shoes off.

204
00:21:49,738 --> 00:21:51,688
You'll feel lighter, too.

205
00:21:51,688 --> 00:21:53,687
Promise.

206
00:21:53,687 --> 00:21:55,589
Go on.

207
00:21:55,589 --> 00:21:57,373
Try it.

208
00:22:00,527 --> 00:22:01,828
See?

209
00:22:01,828 --> 00:22:03,197
The other one too.

210
00:22:04,899 --> 00:22:06,372
How do you feel?

211
00:22:07,235 --> 00:22:09,085
Am I right?

212
00:22:09,085 --> 00:22:12,640
I told you it feels good to go barefoot.
Right?

213
00:22:12,640 --> 00:22:15,243
It feels good to be barefoot.

214
00:22:15,243 --> 00:22:19,067
And what you'll do next is you'll shout.

215
00:22:19,067 --> 00:22:21,017
You're able to breathe now.

216
00:22:21,017 --> 00:22:23,460
Right? You'll shout...

217
00:22:23,460 --> 00:22:25,754
"It feels so good to breathe!"

218
00:22:28,856 --> 00:22:30,967
Try it, go!

219
00:22:32,260 --> 00:22:33,799
Go!

220
00:22:36,164 --> 00:22:38,332
It feels good to breathe!

221
00:22:38,332 --> 00:22:40,475
Louder!

222
00:22:40,475 --> 00:22:42,567
It feels good to breathe!

223
00:22:42,567 --> 00:22:43,704
More!

224
00:22:43,704 --> 00:22:46,111
It feels good to breathe!

225
00:22:46,111 --> 00:22:48,898
It feels good to breathe!

226
00:22:49,552 --> 00:22:51,952
There you go! More!

227
00:22:55,999 --> 00:22:57,318
See?

228
00:22:57,318 --> 00:22:58,927
See?

229
00:23:21,997 --> 00:23:23,681
Dear...

230
00:23:26,249 --> 00:23:28,084
Don't tell me...

231
00:23:29,984 --> 00:23:34,285
you choose him over your own father?

232
00:23:35,123 --> 00:23:37,232
I'm your father.

233
00:23:38,546 --> 00:23:40,493
Don't you love me anymore?

234
00:23:40,493 --> 00:23:43,397
You're pointing a gun at me.

235
00:23:44,292 --> 00:23:47,098
I do, Dad.

236
00:23:47,098 --> 00:23:49,166
I love you.

237
00:23:50,435 --> 00:23:53,671
But Liam is all I have.

238
00:23:55,607 --> 00:23:57,941
You have me.

239
00:23:59,689 --> 00:24:02,689
I've always been there for you.

240
00:24:08,614 --> 00:24:10,068
But...

241
00:24:12,731 --> 00:24:15,032
ever since Mama died...

242
00:24:16,202 --> 00:24:18,420
it was never the same.

243
00:24:19,363 --> 00:24:20,939
With you...

244
00:24:22,033 --> 00:24:23,733
With me.

245
00:24:28,211 --> 00:24:30,420
You have to understand, Dad.

246
00:24:31,052 --> 00:24:33,637
I love Liam.

247
00:24:35,449 --> 00:24:37,920
I love him more than my own life.

248
00:24:42,105 --> 00:24:44,142
Don't say that.

249
00:24:47,124 --> 00:24:48,950
Come here, my child.

250
00:24:50,996 --> 00:24:53,616
Give your dad a hug.

251
00:25:10,676 --> 00:25:12,385
Dad.

252
00:25:13,536 --> 00:25:14,919
- Via!
- Spoiled brat!

253
00:25:14,919 --> 00:25:16,277
Via!

254
00:25:17,088 --> 00:25:19,523
What do you know about love?

255
00:25:20,792 --> 00:25:22,928
Dad, please, no! Don't, don't, please!

256
00:25:22,928 --> 00:25:25,731
No, not Liam, please.

257
00:25:25,731 --> 00:25:26,932
Please, not Liam.

258
00:25:26,932 --> 00:25:29,094
Please, Dad.

259
00:25:29,094 --> 00:25:30,469
Don't! Stop it!

260
00:25:30,469 --> 00:25:32,571
Stop!

261
00:25:32,571 --> 00:25:34,516
Stop, please.

262
00:25:34,516 --> 00:25:38,009
That man is already worthless.

263
00:25:39,441 --> 00:25:42,474
That's the problem with you!

264
00:25:42,474 --> 00:25:46,103
Everyone should be useful to you!

265
00:25:46,842 --> 00:25:49,622
Is it not enough that Liam is my boyfriend?

266
00:25:49,622 --> 00:25:51,664
I love him!

267
00:25:53,893 --> 00:25:55,542
Get out of here!

268
00:25:56,179 --> 00:25:59,580
Stop it! Stop!

269
00:25:59,580 --> 00:26:02,048
Love, love...

270
00:26:10,305 --> 00:26:13,711
Dad, do you think we're different?

271
00:26:18,712 --> 00:26:21,882
You're acting like that...

272
00:26:21,882 --> 00:26:26,449
You think about nothing but power and money

273
00:26:26,449 --> 00:26:29,384
because you lost Mom.

274
00:26:31,024 --> 00:26:33,066
Don't you drag your mom into this.

275
00:26:33,066 --> 00:26:35,101
Am I wrong?

276
00:26:37,095 --> 00:26:45,619
Ever since Mom died,
I have lost you, too, Dad.

277
00:26:47,041 --> 00:26:49,405
I was all alone.

278
00:26:50,427 --> 00:26:54,106
I've never felt so alone in my whole life.

279
00:26:55,508 --> 00:26:59,078
I used to always think...

280
00:27:00,671 --> 00:27:04,440
that I should have gone with Mom.

281
00:27:08,303 --> 00:27:11,100
That only changed because of Liam.

282
00:27:14,867 --> 00:27:17,116
Because of Liam.

283
00:27:19,221 --> 00:27:24,794
I hold on to my life
because of what he made me feel.

284
00:27:25,748 --> 00:27:29,705
So if you want to take him away from me, go!

285
00:27:29,705 --> 00:27:31,420
Go ahead.

286
00:27:31,420 --> 00:27:33,381
Kill me first.

287
00:27:44,204 --> 00:27:46,903
Dad! Dad, stop!

288
00:27:46,903 --> 00:27:48,402
From now on,

289
00:27:49,418 --> 00:27:55,678
you are no longer connected
to any of my businesses.

290
00:27:55,678 --> 00:28:00,608
You won't have a say in
any of our transactions.

291
00:28:01,784 --> 00:28:05,398
If you give me problems,

292
00:28:05,398 --> 00:28:13,297
I will hurt not you,
but the people who matter to you.

293
00:28:13,297 --> 00:28:14,832
That's enough, Dad. Stop.

294
00:28:14,832 --> 00:28:15,901
Just go.

295
00:28:15,901 --> 00:28:19,124
- Go, go.
- Remember this.

296
00:28:19,124 --> 00:28:23,869
You'll regret staying alive.

297
00:28:25,582 --> 00:28:26,824
Love.

298
00:28:27,513 --> 00:28:28,979
Love.

299
00:28:28,979 --> 00:28:30,716
Love, love...

300
00:28:31,540 --> 00:28:33,017
Via.

301
00:28:35,709 --> 00:28:37,065
Via.

302
00:28:38,322 --> 00:28:40,157
I'm sorry.

303
00:28:40,157 --> 00:28:42,875
I'm sorry.

304
00:28:42,875 --> 00:28:45,176
I'm sorry, love.

305
00:29:01,657 --> 00:29:03,782
I'm sorry.

306
00:29:03,782 --> 00:29:05,675
I'm sorry...

307
00:29:28,557 --> 00:29:30,232
You're really strong.

308
00:29:31,351 --> 00:29:33,417
And cut!

309
00:29:33,417 --> 00:29:35,949
- Cut!
- Yeah, hit him!

310
00:29:36,671 --> 00:29:38,026
It's already cut!

311
00:29:38,026 --> 00:29:39,862
He doesn't run out of...

312
00:29:39,862 --> 00:29:41,653
It's already cut.

313
00:29:41,653 --> 00:29:43,833
That's enough.

314
00:29:43,833 --> 00:29:45,759
He has lots of energy.

315
00:29:45,759 --> 00:29:48,035
I think you have to go home.

316
00:29:48,035 --> 00:29:50,296
I want to be an action star.

317
00:29:51,418 --> 00:29:52,730
Action star.

318
00:29:52,730 --> 00:29:55,268
That's enough. It's already late.

319
00:29:55,268 --> 00:29:59,005
I think you need to go home.
You're already sleepy.

320
00:29:59,005 --> 00:30:00,255
Where's Sir Liam?

321
00:30:00,255 --> 00:30:02,341
He can instruct the service vehicle
to bring you home.

322
00:30:02,341 --> 00:30:04,689
- Borj, where's...
- Boss Bro?

323
00:30:04,689 --> 00:30:09,931
Miss Joyce, I was with Sir Liam earlier
while waiting for the props.

324
00:30:09,931 --> 00:30:12,649
But when I returned to greet the suppliers,

325
00:30:12,649 --> 00:30:14,742
Sir Liam wasn't there anymore.

326
00:30:15,502 --> 00:30:18,356
Maybe VLH called him over to Blacksmith.

327
00:30:18,356 --> 00:30:22,888
How about this?
Did you see VLH's face when he saw my boss?

328
00:30:22,888 --> 00:30:27,431
He was fuming mad like a dragon.

329
00:30:27,431 --> 00:30:28,481
That's true.

330
00:30:28,481 --> 00:30:33,040
I almost called the firefighters
because I thought he would spit fire.

331
00:30:33,040 --> 00:30:34,966
Excuse me, Madam Megan...

332
00:30:34,966 --> 00:30:39,076
But it is such a waste how your boss
is good-looking but grumpy.

333
00:30:39,076 --> 00:30:41,088
Silly.

334
00:30:41,088 --> 00:30:45,714
Sep, dear. Do you want me to
bring you back to the orphanage?

335
00:30:45,714 --> 00:30:49,396
Miss Joyce,
I still want to watch the filming.

336
00:30:49,396 --> 00:30:51,587
One more take.

337
00:30:52,255 --> 00:30:54,261
Do you still want to watch our filming?

338
00:30:54,261 --> 00:30:55,923
One last take, okay?

339
00:30:55,923 --> 00:30:58,161
Promise? And then you'll go home.

340
00:30:58,161 --> 00:30:59,773
Okay, one more.

341
00:30:59,773 --> 00:31:02,486
- One more. One more.
- Alright, one more.

342
00:31:02,486 --> 00:31:03,583
Give some punches.

343
00:31:03,583 --> 00:31:04,468
- Go, Sep!
- Go, Sep!

344
00:31:04,468 --> 00:31:05,635
- Go, Sep!
- Go, Sep!

345
00:31:05,635 --> 00:31:07,596
- Go!
- Energy!

346
00:31:12,000 --> 00:31:15,582
- He has lots of energy...
- Superman.

347
00:31:15,582 --> 00:31:16,706
What's wrong?

348
00:31:16,706 --> 00:31:18,148
What's going on?

349
00:31:18,148 --> 00:31:19,501
He's not acting anymore!

350
00:31:19,501 --> 00:31:20,921
- Sep!
- Call a medic!

351
00:31:20,921 --> 00:31:23,056
- Sep, what's wrong?
- Sep...

352
00:31:23,056 --> 00:31:24,924
Sep.

353
00:31:24,924 --> 00:31:27,458
- Medic!
- Medic!

354
00:31:27,458 --> 00:31:29,092
Here, here!

355
00:31:32,599 --> 00:31:34,003
Via.

356
00:31:36,069 --> 00:31:39,955
You shouldn't have intervened.

357
00:31:42,708 --> 00:31:46,245
No. I meant everything I said.

358
00:31:48,589 --> 00:31:53,174
I can't lose you, Liam.

359
00:31:53,174 --> 00:31:55,912
But based on what I heard,

360
00:31:58,158 --> 00:32:04,797
you know that your dad is mad at me...

361
00:32:07,077 --> 00:32:10,216
because of our real business.

362
00:32:21,014 --> 00:32:22,610
I lied.

363
00:32:25,418 --> 00:32:29,822
I lied when I said...

364
00:32:30,803 --> 00:32:33,941
I didn't know about my dad's business.

365
00:32:36,311 --> 00:32:38,189
I know everything.

366
00:32:39,777 --> 00:32:42,415
The illegal ones, too.

367
00:32:42,415 --> 00:32:45,337
But it doesn't matter anymore.

368
00:32:46,673 --> 00:32:51,371
What's important is that he let you go.

369
00:32:54,647 --> 00:32:57,783
We can put that behind us now.

370
00:32:58,604 --> 00:33:01,373
We can start over again.

371
00:33:11,580 --> 00:33:13,337
Thank you...

372
00:33:14,987 --> 00:33:16,710
Love.

373
00:33:30,259 --> 00:33:32,006
Everything's okay now.

374
00:33:43,634 --> 00:33:44,953
Love.

375
00:33:47,167 --> 00:33:51,041
[5 Missed Calls]
[8 Messages]

376
00:33:51,042 --> 00:33:54,097
[Sep collapsed at the set.]

377
00:33:54,097 --> 00:33:55,542
It's Sep.

378
00:33:57,075 --> 00:33:58,256
Wait, wait.

379
00:33:58,256 --> 00:34:01,454
- I can do it.
- Be careful.

380
00:34:01,454 --> 00:34:03,016
Wait. Wait.

381
00:34:03,016 --> 00:34:04,284
Don't force it, please.

382
00:34:04,284 --> 00:34:06,051
- Don't force it.
- I can do it.

383
00:34:08,521 --> 00:34:09,832
Wait.

384
00:34:20,533 --> 00:34:22,401
Slowly.

385
00:34:28,074 --> 00:34:29,557
Joyce.

386
00:34:30,729 --> 00:34:33,746
Liam, what happened to you?

387
00:34:33,746 --> 00:34:36,149
This is nothing. I'm okay.

388
00:34:36,149 --> 00:34:38,051
Are you okay? You don't look okay.

389
00:34:38,051 --> 00:34:40,119
Where's Sep?

390
00:34:42,255 --> 00:34:44,223
He's okay, Joyce.

391
00:34:45,298 --> 00:34:46,558
Where's Sep?

392
00:34:46,558 --> 00:34:48,261
How's his condition?

393
00:34:48,261 --> 00:34:50,528
He's inside.

394
00:35:03,852 --> 00:35:05,178
Sep.

395
00:35:05,178 --> 00:35:06,534
Sister.

396
00:35:07,336 --> 00:35:10,315
Sep, how are you? How are you feeling?

397
00:35:11,784 --> 00:35:14,454
Sir Liam, I'm okay.

398
00:35:14,454 --> 00:35:18,157
Looks like you're the one
who should go to the hospital.

399
00:35:18,157 --> 00:35:21,294
Is that real or just makeup?

400
00:35:21,294 --> 00:35:23,429
This is just makeup. Don't worry about me.

401
00:35:23,429 --> 00:35:25,547
I'm okay.

402
00:35:25,547 --> 00:35:28,734
You should regain your strength.
What happened to you?

403
00:35:31,264 --> 00:35:37,509
I'm sorry. If I knew you were together,
I wouldn't bother Liam.

404
00:35:38,850 --> 00:35:40,557
It's fine.

405
00:35:40,557 --> 00:35:43,410
Liam loves the kid.

406
00:35:44,350 --> 00:35:48,453
I know he'll beat himself up
if something bad happens to Sep.

407
00:36:08,382 --> 00:36:10,193
- Sir Liam.
- Yes?

408
00:36:10,193 --> 00:36:16,728
Can you be an action star
even if you have a weak heart?

409
00:36:16,728 --> 00:36:20,252
Sep has a heart disease.

410
00:36:20,252 --> 00:36:22,754
He got it from his father.

411
00:36:22,754 --> 00:36:25,924
The doctor has seen him already.

412
00:36:25,924 --> 00:36:28,593
He said Sep needed to rest.

413
00:36:28,593 --> 00:36:31,629
He already took his medicines.

414
00:36:33,491 --> 00:36:35,634
Sister.

415
00:36:35,634 --> 00:36:38,270
I'm sorry, Sister.

416
00:36:38,270 --> 00:36:42,249
I'm sorry Sep got tired in our set.

417
00:36:42,249 --> 00:36:44,509
If I only knew...

418
00:36:44,509 --> 00:36:47,153
No one wanted this to happen, dear.

419
00:36:48,375 --> 00:36:50,715
Don't worry.

420
00:36:50,715 --> 00:36:54,652
I'm okay. I can still do TikTok.

421
00:36:56,688 --> 00:36:58,490
Is that TikTok?

422
00:36:58,490 --> 00:37:00,825
What kind of move is that? Ouch.

423
00:37:00,825 --> 00:37:02,827
You're heavy.

424
00:37:02,827 --> 00:37:04,628
Are you okay?

425
00:37:07,999 --> 00:37:09,800
How about me?

426
00:37:14,306 --> 00:37:18,176
I know the best cardiologist in Manila.

427
00:37:18,176 --> 00:37:22,780
I can give him a call. So we can be sure.

428
00:37:28,042 --> 00:37:30,322
Yes, please...

429
00:37:33,758 --> 00:37:35,088
Love.

430
00:37:38,330 --> 00:37:39,958
I'll call him.

431
00:38:16,468 --> 00:38:18,680
That's deep.

432
00:38:33,395 --> 00:38:34,887
Joyce.

433
00:38:36,203 --> 00:38:38,273
Don't get mad at me.

434
00:38:40,901 --> 00:38:43,162
This time...

435
00:38:43,162 --> 00:38:46,155
It is not my choice anymore.

436
00:38:46,155 --> 00:38:47,856
What do you mean?

437
00:38:49,620 --> 00:38:52,055
I was gone earlier...

438
00:38:54,408 --> 00:38:59,204
because I received news...

439
00:38:59,204 --> 00:39:02,674
that I was kicked out from
the Herrera Group of Companies.

440
00:39:04,097 --> 00:39:06,505
That means...

441
00:39:06,505 --> 00:39:08,873
I'm no longer part of Blacksmith.

442
00:39:10,288 --> 00:39:13,357
I can't go back to Casa Fuerte either.

443
00:39:16,223 --> 00:39:20,042
Is that how mad your father is?

444
00:39:20,042 --> 00:39:25,088
That you chose the film over Casa Fuerte?

445
00:39:28,270 --> 00:39:31,172
I went against a major investor.

446
00:39:36,855 --> 00:39:39,323
What will happen to our movie?

447
00:39:42,487 --> 00:39:44,341
You're no longer part of our project?

448
00:39:44,341 --> 00:39:47,243
You're done after the first filming?

449
00:39:48,102 --> 00:39:52,839
I have no choice but to start over again.

450
00:40:04,113 --> 00:40:07,615
Why don't we make our own film?

451
00:40:09,118 --> 00:40:10,568
What?

452
00:40:11,804 --> 00:40:14,315
What about your film with Josh at Blacksmith?

453
00:40:14,315 --> 00:40:15,788
Liam...

454
00:40:16,875 --> 00:40:20,536
You're the reason I accepted that project.

455
00:40:20,536 --> 00:40:25,281
Because of your talent, vision,
and dedication.

456
00:40:25,281 --> 00:40:26,903
You.

457
00:40:29,917 --> 00:40:34,467
I know about the deal you made
with your father and Congressman Ramon.

458
00:40:37,519 --> 00:40:40,121
Josh told me about it.

459
00:40:42,250 --> 00:40:45,920
Maybe that project isn't really for me.

460
00:40:45,920 --> 00:40:48,889
Maybe we are just forcing it.

461
00:40:51,059 --> 00:40:55,630
Joyce... I don't want you to be impulsive.

462
00:40:55,630 --> 00:40:59,066
I'm not being impulsive.

463
00:41:00,368 --> 00:41:04,275
I'm telling you right now
that I want us to make a movie.

464
00:41:04,275 --> 00:41:07,414
Make sure you'll give me creative freedom.

465
00:41:07,414 --> 00:41:10,791
And on one condition.

466
00:41:11,713 --> 00:41:18,620
Part of what we'll make from the movie
will go to this orphanage.

467
00:41:18,620 --> 00:41:21,842
I've already fallen in love
with the kids here.

468
00:41:22,624 --> 00:41:25,400
Especially with Sep.

469
00:41:26,414 --> 00:41:28,653
He has become important to me.

470
00:41:31,266 --> 00:41:34,702
Joyce, I won't say no to that.

471
00:41:36,070 --> 00:41:37,545
Deal?

472
00:41:40,175 --> 00:41:41,956
Deal.

473
00:42:29,629 --> 00:42:31,337
My friend.

474
00:42:31,337 --> 00:42:34,042
Why did you suddenly want to see me?

475
00:42:45,871 --> 00:42:47,387
What is this?

476
00:42:48,756 --> 00:42:50,413
Open it.

477
00:43:09,060 --> 00:43:11,863
What's this for, Congressman?

478
00:43:11,863 --> 00:43:16,201
That's money collected from
my cockpit arenas in the province.

479
00:43:16,201 --> 00:43:23,341
Use that money for the new subdivisions
that Casa Fuerte is developing.

480
00:43:24,609 --> 00:43:27,078
And from now on...

481
00:43:27,078 --> 00:43:31,349
you'll take the jobs Liam used to do.

482
00:43:31,349 --> 00:43:34,352
Why? What did you do to my son?

483
00:43:35,887 --> 00:43:38,423
Don't worry.

484
00:43:38,423 --> 00:43:40,524
Your son is alive.

485
00:43:41,500 --> 00:43:44,729
You have to thank my daughter.

486
00:43:44,729 --> 00:43:48,266
Because if not for Via,

487
00:43:48,266 --> 00:43:54,338
it would have been Liam's head
in that bag instead of money.

488
00:43:57,380 --> 00:44:01,583
And you'll have to do the next collection.

489
00:44:02,934 --> 00:44:04,382
What can you do?

490
00:44:05,396 --> 00:44:09,340
Your favorite son abandoned you.

491
00:44:21,066 --> 00:44:24,769
Here are the copies
of our sequence breakdown.

492
00:44:26,171 --> 00:44:27,906
One for you...

493
00:44:27,906 --> 00:44:30,074
One for you.

494
00:44:30,976 --> 00:44:32,110
Give that to me.

495
00:44:32,110 --> 00:44:33,979
The one you're holding. Let me have it.

496
00:44:33,979 --> 00:44:34,980
Give me that.

497
00:44:34,980 --> 00:44:36,081
Give me that.

498
00:44:36,081 --> 00:44:37,915
Josh, let me have that.

499
00:44:39,351 --> 00:44:40,800
Give me that.

500
00:44:46,291 --> 00:44:48,193
New direction.

501
00:44:48,193 --> 00:44:49,928
I saw the scenes you already shot.

502
00:44:49,928 --> 00:44:51,463
I didn't like it.

503
00:44:51,463 --> 00:44:53,431
It's so disappointing!

504
00:44:53,431 --> 00:44:57,335
I want our hero to be very manly.

505
00:44:57,335 --> 00:44:59,604
He must have swag.

506
00:44:59,604 --> 00:45:01,272
Guys, imagine this...

507
00:45:01,272 --> 00:45:04,809
<i>Our hero is running with a leather jacket on.</i>

508
00:45:04,809 --> 00:45:09,614
He's holding the hand of his leading lady,
a sexy woman.

509
00:45:09,614 --> 00:45:11,049
This is an action scene.

510
00:45:11,049 --> 00:45:14,686
But, of course,
our hero is good at fight scenes.

511
00:45:19,718 --> 00:45:24,837
<i>He will protect his helpless leading lady.</i>

512
00:45:38,376 --> 00:45:39,924
Help!

513
00:45:44,149 --> 00:45:47,875
<i>And then, he will defeat all the enemies.</i>

514
00:45:55,178 --> 00:46:00,318
<i>And they slowly kiss.</i>

515
00:46:11,042 --> 00:46:12,804
No!

516
00:46:14,679 --> 00:46:16,748
That's what I want to see.

517
00:46:16,748 --> 00:46:19,483
That's the kind of film
that will make him win the elections.

518
00:46:20,785 --> 00:46:28,093
VLH, maybe it's better
if the leading lady can fight.

519
00:46:28,093 --> 00:46:31,129
Imagine a fight scene like this.

520
00:46:32,363 --> 00:46:36,401
<i>The hero and his leading lady
are both fighting.</i>

521
00:46:36,401 --> 00:46:39,037
<i>Let's show
that the woman knows how to use nunchuck...</i>

522
00:46:39,037 --> 00:46:40,972
<i>That she can also fight.</i>

523
00:46:43,942 --> 00:46:46,878
<i>There's no difference
between a man and a woman.</i>

524
00:46:46,878 --> 00:46:51,013
<i>When it comes to fighting,
all you need is heart and skills.</i>

525
00:46:57,413 --> 00:46:59,157
Wait, VLH.

526
00:46:59,157 --> 00:47:00,917
What happened to the original story?

527
00:47:00,918 --> 00:47:04,707
We insisted on having an empowered heroine
in the movie, right?

528
00:47:04,707 --> 00:47:07,966
And it goes well with my political platform
as vice mayor.

529
00:47:07,966 --> 00:47:09,634
Women's rights,

530
00:47:09,634 --> 00:47:12,670
as well as the rights of the LGBT community.

531
00:47:12,670 --> 00:47:14,252
Vice mayor?

532
00:47:14,252 --> 00:47:15,940
I thought you'd run for Congress?

533
00:47:15,940 --> 00:47:21,446
Uncle Ramon told me to run as vice mayor
of my hometown for now,

534
00:47:21,446 --> 00:47:24,649
because it will be a sure win.

535
00:47:24,649 --> 00:47:27,819
It's up to you what position you want.

536
00:47:27,819 --> 00:47:32,490
But we shouldn't narrow down
the demographic your film can reach.

537
00:47:32,490 --> 00:47:35,660
Josh, your male voters will get turned off.

538
00:47:35,660 --> 00:47:40,005
To make the hero stronger,
the woman should be weak.

539
00:47:43,168 --> 00:47:45,012
Well...

540
00:47:46,771 --> 00:47:49,288
I guess I'm right.

541
00:47:50,809 --> 00:47:56,647
I think this film is not for me anymore.

542
00:47:58,850 --> 00:48:00,751
Sorry.

543
00:48:01,686 --> 00:48:06,191
I don't want to hurt anyone,

544
00:48:06,191 --> 00:48:08,669
but I've already made a decision.

545
00:48:10,911 --> 00:48:13,670
I won't do this film anymore.

546
00:48:15,200 --> 00:48:19,234
I will buy out my contract.

547
00:48:21,706 --> 00:48:26,344
If you have any questions,
you can talk to my lawyer.

548
00:48:26,344 --> 00:48:29,372
Actually, I can recommend

549
00:48:29,372 --> 00:48:34,185
a leading lady who will be eager
to accept this project...

550
00:48:34,185 --> 00:48:38,216
Especially the story you want, VLH.

551
00:48:39,858 --> 00:48:44,187
Again, I... I'm sorry.

552
00:48:45,363 --> 00:48:48,365
And thanks to all of you.

553
00:48:49,844 --> 00:48:51,439
And Josh...

554
00:48:54,405 --> 00:48:55,874
Good luck.

555
00:49:17,262 --> 00:49:19,963
Is Maxine busy right now?

556
00:49:41,953 --> 00:49:45,089
Aunt Tess, this is Hans, my friend.

557
00:49:45,089 --> 00:49:47,025
You look good together.

558
00:49:47,025 --> 00:49:49,994
Liam, your family owns Casa Fuerte, right?

559
00:49:49,994 --> 00:49:51,996
- Yes.
- An accident happened

560
00:49:51,996 --> 00:49:53,231
at your construction site.

561
00:49:53,231 --> 00:49:54,632
They want me to handle the case.

562
00:49:54,632 --> 00:49:56,401
Did someone die in Casa Fuerte?

563
00:49:56,401 --> 00:49:58,536
I'm surrounded by stupid people!

564
00:49:58,536 --> 00:49:59,971
Spare me, Ramon.

565
00:49:59,971 --> 00:50:01,673
I'm just new here.

566
00:50:01,673 --> 00:50:04,442
That's why I need veterans.

567
00:50:04,442 --> 00:50:07,879
This is Lando, my most trusted gunman.

568
00:50:07,879 --> 00:50:12,884
You'll see his face last
if you fail again, Danilo.

569
00:50:12,884 --> 00:50:15,764
Why did you have to get

570
00:50:15,764 --> 00:50:17,956
the black sheep of the Herreras
for a boyfriend?

571
00:50:17,956 --> 00:50:19,657
You could have gotten Vergil instead.

572
00:50:19,657 --> 00:50:23,061
Mom, are you still concerned about money?

573
00:50:23,061 --> 00:50:24,495
This is not about money.

574
00:50:24,495 --> 00:50:25,863
This is about your career.

575
00:50:25,863 --> 00:50:28,691
I have my own mind.

576
00:50:28,691 --> 00:50:30,802
You stepped on me.

577
00:50:30,802 --> 00:50:33,071
That's why you're not on the ground.

578
00:50:33,071 --> 00:50:35,173
I'll let you indulge in your craziness.

579
00:50:35,173 --> 00:50:38,376
But the next time you sign a contract,

580
00:50:38,376 --> 00:50:41,813
you will do it even if it comes from a demon.

581
00:50:41,813 --> 00:50:43,081
It's not too late.

582
00:50:43,081 --> 00:50:44,615
We can still break away
from Congressman Ramon.

583
00:50:44,615 --> 00:50:48,252
I know I wasn't the best father
to you and your sibling.
